ly their own orders, never another buyer's orders.\",\n     \"3: When the buyer has no orders, 'No orders yet' is shown with a link to Find parts.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Orders in status Placed can be cancelled by the buyer (with confirmation) setting status to Cancelled; order detail shows a status timeline (Placed→Packed→Dispatched→Delivered) plus a status filter on the list.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Selecting a status filter on My orders shows only orders matching that status.\",\n     \"1: Opening an order shows its lines, delivery address, delivery option, total, and a status timeline Placed → Packed → Dispatched → Delivered.\",\n     \"2: While status is Placed, a 'Cancel order' button is shown; pressing it and confirming sets the order status to Cancelled.\",\n     \"3: 'Cancel order' button is not shown once status has progressed past Placed (Packed, Dispatched, Delivered, or already Cancelled).\",\n     \"4: Cancelling without confirming the action leaves the order status unchanged.\",\n     \"5: Cancelled status is reflected both in the orders list and the order detail timeline (e.g., as a distinct terminal state, not part of the Placed→Delivered progression).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-7\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Full WCAG 2.1 AA compliance (keyboard operability, labelled fields, non-colour-only signalling) and responsive layout from 360px width upward across all three screens.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All interactive elements (search, filters, quantity fields, buttons, links) are operable via keyboard alone.\",\n     \"1: Every form field (search box, quantity, address, delivery option, status filter) has an associated accessible label.\",\n     \"2: Stock state and order status are conveyed with text/icons, never colour alone.\",\n     \"3: All three screens render usably on viewport widths from 360px (phone) up to desktop widths.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I